  "question": {
    "text": "Two parabolas with a common vertex and with axes along the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>-axis respectively, intersect each other in the first quadrant. If the length of the latus rectum of each parabola is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>, then the equation of the common tangent to the two parabolas is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "a2GnF",
      "text": "<math><mi> </mi><mn>3</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZdSJI",
      "text": "<math><mn>8</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "c7xt9",
      "text": "<math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "VZru8",
      "text": "<math><mn>4</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Equation of two parabola are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi></math>.</p><p>Let equation of tangent to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is also tangent to <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi></math></p><p><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><msup><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> have equal roots</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>144</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Hence, common tangent is <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>4</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>",
